        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2010",
        "question_text": "<p>Find the coefficient of $x^3$ in the expansion of $(2x - 3)^5$.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Use the binomial expansion formula: $(a + b)^n = \\sum_{k=0}^{n} \\binom{n}{k} a^{n-k} b^k$.<br><br>Here, $a = 2x$, $b = -3$, and $n = 5$. The general term is $\\binom{5}{k} (2x)^{5-k} (-3)^k$.<br><br>For the coefficient of $x^3$, set $5 - k = 3 \\Rightarrow k = 2$.<br><br>The coefficient is $\\binom{5}{2} (2)^{3} (-3)^2 = 10 \\times 8 \\times 9 = 720$.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
