        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2010",
        "question_text": "<p>Find the derivative of $y = x^3 \\ln x$ with respect to $x$.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Use the product rule: $\\frac{dy}{dx} = u \\frac{dv}{dx} + v \\frac{du}{dx}$, where $u = x^3$ and $v = \\ln x$.<br><br>$\\frac{du}{dx} = 3x^2$, $\\frac{dv}{dx} = \\frac{1}{x}$.<br><br>Thus, $\\frac{dy}{dx} = x^3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{x} + \\ln x \\cdot 3x^2 = x^2 + 3x^2 \\ln x$.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
